-- Ordered quest guidance; source 967020b2b8ca645afcaf90d9bbe5a1b64673947d; generated 2026-10-20.
QuestGuidance.Register("en",424,{
[13537]="7002C223\n1\tDefeat Nink-hai sentries (total: 4)\030Defeat Nink-hai skirmishers (total: 3)\030Defeat Nink-hai ravagers (total: 3)\tThe tribe of Orc-vandals is south-west of the Cuthstan. Lanbert has asked you to thin out the numbers of the Orc-tribe, in the hopes of scaring them from the area.\n2\tTalk to Lanbert at the Cuthstan-camp\tLanbert is at the Rohirrim-camp at the base of the Cuthstan. You have thinned the numbers of the Orc-tribe, and Lanbert awaits your return.\n",
[13538]="7001ABE8\n1\tDefeat Dirk Hawthorn\tDirk Hawthorn is on the south side of the ruined wall at the foot of the hills surrounding the Barrow-downs, east of Adso's Camp. Adso fears that the brigand leader, Dirk Hawthorn, will return and kill his workers in the night and asked you to deal with this threat before he could follow through.\n2\tTalk to Adso Haybank\tAdso awaits your return at his camp along the Great East Road. The brigands at the ruined wall proved to be no true threat and were dispatched with ease.\n",
[13539]="700588A9\n1\tDefeat Grush-and-Flak\tA fearsome two-headed troll Grush-and-Flak has been attacking a wide array of troops throughout the countryside. Find the creature and drive it from the battlefield.\n2\tDefeat Grush-and-Flak\tThe fearsome two-headed troll Grush-and-Flak has been attacking a wide array of troops throughout the countryside. Find the creature and drive it from the battlefield.\n3\tSpeak to Hlóthi\tLet Hlóthi know that Grush-and-Flak has been driven off.\n",
[13540]="700588A7\n1\tDefeat Hoshkhor\tHoshkhor, has become known to the gathered forces of Gabil'akkâ. This foul captain has routed several patrols throughout the area and has hindered supply lines for the war effort.\n2\tDefeat Hoshkhor\tHoshkhor has become known to the gathered forces of Gabil'akkâ. This foul creature has routed several patrols throughout the area and has hindered supply lines for the war effort.\n3\tSpeak to Hlóthi\tHoshkhor has become known to the gathered forces of Gabil'akkâ. This foul creature has routed several patrols throughout the area and has hindered supply lines for the war effort.\n",
[13541]="700588A8\n1\tDefeat Mozlut\tMozlut is an enormous Warg who has been rampaging across the battlefield. Drive off this foul beast.\n2\tDefeat Mozlut\tMozlut is an enormous Warg who has been rampaging across the battlefield. Drive off this foul beast.\n3\tSpeak to Hlóthi\tFind Hlóthi and inform him that you were able to drive off the beast.\n",
[13542]="700588A6\n1\tDefeat Svalblóth\tA foul drake that goes by Svalblóth has emerged from Gundabad. The survivors from several patrols claim that this creature ate half of their group and continued to maraud across the battlefield.\n2\tDrive off Svalblóth\tA foul drake that goes by Svalblóth has emerged from Gundabad. The survivors from several patrols claim that this creature ate half of their group and continued to maraud across the battlefield.\n3\tSpeak to Hlóthi\tWith Svalblóth driven off, return to Hlóthi, and let him know that deed has been done.\n",
[13543]="7005AAAC\n1\tComplete 'The Tombs of Akhaldarâg' from Ausma\030Complete 'Lair of the Frost-horde' from Ausma\030Complete 'The Camps of Stazg Vozag' from Ausma\tScout-master Ausma's apprentices have been sent to points of interest around the Pit of Stonejaws. You should find Kyrstig, Molkha, and Klúso and assist them with their missions.\n2\tTalk to Scout-master Ausma\tYou have aided the dwarf scouts with their missions. You should talk to Scout-master Ausma in Bárgstad.\n",
[13544]="7005AAF4\n1\tDefeat Orc-kind in Thyrstáth (total: 15)\tThe Orcs and hobgoblins are engaged in a battle in the ice-giant settlement. You should defeat Orc-kind in Thyrstáth.\n2\tCall Hórin and talk to him\tUse the summoning horn to call Hórin to your side. You should talk to Hórin.\n",
[13545]="7004A39C\n1\tHail the Easterlings before Rhûd Vorn\tYou should hail the Easterlings as Kurtil taught you before their camp, Rhûd Vorn, on the northern slopes of Udûn.\n2\tTalk to the Easterling Lord\tYou should talk to the Easterling Lord who responded to your hailing, outside Rhûd Vorn, on the northern slopes of Udûn.\n3\tFind the great banner\030Find the letter\030Bring Yordam to the Black Gate\tYou should lead Yordam the Easterling to a view of the Black Gates, the Great Flag on the parade grounds, and seek the letter dispatched to Maudhúl Vôr. If you get separated from Yordam, wind his horn to call him back to you.\n4\tTalk to Yordam\tNow that you have found the fallen banner, the dead letter-bearer, and the Black Gates broken, you should talk to Yordam. If you get separated from Yordam, wind his horn to call him back to you.\n5\tReturn to Khôpol\tNow that you have collected the proofs, you should return to Khôpol before Rhûd Vorn, on the northern slopes of Udûn.\n6\tReturn to Kurtil\tHaving secured the pledge from the Easterling Lord Khôpol, you should return to Kurtil and the other forge-workers where they had been, on the height above Maudhúl Vôr.\n",
[13546]="7000F1DC\n1\tFind Burgthryth's first sheet\tBurgthryth believes the first of her sheets was swiped from her pack by a Tundra Bear. You will have to hunt them down until you find the one that stole it -- assuming it has not already been devoured. Tundra Bears can be found in Länsi-mâ.\n2\tFind Burgthryth's second sheet\tBurgthryth told you that the second of her anthem sheets might have been grabbed by a curious peikko during her performance. You will have to hunt down the peikko that stole it. Many Peikko may be found in a small cave due east of Zigilgund.\n3\tFind Burgthryth's third sheet\tBurgthryth thinks she probably dropped the third sheet of her anthem when she was being pursued by Gauradan-hunters. You will have to hunt down the Gauredain and retrieve that sheet before they use it as a hankerchief -- or worse. Gauredain can be found in Länsi-mâ.\n4\tBring Burgthryth's anthem sheets to her at Jänis-leiri\tBurgthryth is at Jänis-leiri. You finally found all the sheets of Burgthryth's scattered anthem. You will need to return them to her at once.\n",
[13547]="7001758D\n1\tReturn to Dithrik in the Foundations of Stone\030Collect Nameless heads (total: 12)\tThe Nameless beings and the ancient creature prowl the vicinity of the Foundations of Stone, especially to the south-east of this region. Dithrik has asked you to collect twelve unspoiled heads from the Nameless of the Foundations of Stone.\n",
[13548]="7004CF01\n1\tTalk to Karst\tBy completing this quest, you will automatically complete any unfinished Throne of the Dread Terror meta deeds and receive raid tokens and Ancient Ithil-coins.\n",
[13549]="7003081D\n1\tDefeat mounted Orcs from the East Wall (total: 6)\tOrc Warg-riders can be found near the stream to the north-west of Walstow and along the sides of the road west to Snowbourn.\n2\tCompleted\tYou have defeated the mounted riders and beaten back the renewed assault from the East Wall.\n",
[13550]="70046C3E\n1\tFollow the western roadway northward from Cair Andros\tCair Andros can be found on the Anduin in north-western North Ithilien and its road leads northward towards Dagorlad. Jarl Gurthilm has asked you to follow the western roadway northward through Ithilien and follow his company to the Khundolar encampment.\n2\tFollow the roadway northward towards Dagorlad\tThe roadway north can be found far to north-west of Henneth Annûn. You are following the roadway and should continue to follow Jarl Gurthilm's company to the Khundolar encampment.\n3\tContinue to follow the roadway towards Dagorlad\tThe roadway north can be found far to north-west of Henneth Annûn. You are following the roadway and should continue to follow Jarl Gurthilm's company to the Khundolar encampment.\n4\tFollow the roadway eastward towards Uya Hujûm\tThe roadway travels eastward through North Ithilien can be found to the north of Henneth Annûn. The roadway has forked eastward and you should continue to follow Jarl Gurthilm's company to the Khundolar encampment.\n5\tFollow the roadway eastward towards Uya Hujûm\tThe roadway travels eastward through North Ithilien can be found to the north of Henneth Annûn. The roadway has forked eastward and you should continue to follow Jarl Gurthilm's company to the Khundolar encampment.\n6\tFind Jarl Gurthilm and his company near Uya Hujûm\tJarl Gurthilm and his company can be found to the south-east of Uya Hujûm. You have followed Jarl Gurthilm's company to a trail of dead and should now seek the Variag company nearby.\n7\tTalk to Jarl Gurthilm outside Uya Hujûm\tJarl Gurthilm can be found in north-eastern North Ithilien at the foot of Uya Hujûm. You have found Jarl Gurthilm and his company and should now speak to him.\n",
[13551]="70044E41\n1\tTalk to Rhus Cornchúthur at the entrance to Maur Tulhau\030Talk to Iola Isbrun at the entrance to Maur Tulhau\tBingo is saying his farewells to the hobbits of Maur Tulhau, and said he would meet you at the southern exit of the village.\n2\tTalk to Bingo at the entrance to Maur Tulhau\tBingo is at the entrance to Maur Tulhau, in the Gloomglens. Bingo has said his good-byes and is now ready to continue his northern journey.\n3\tTalk to Bingo at the entrance to Maur Tulhau and continue the journey north\tBingo is at the entrance to Maur Tulhau, in the Gloomglens. Bingo has said his good-byes and is now ready to continue his northern journey.\n4\tTalk to Bingo in the Andrath\tBingo has passed through the blockade and is now in the Andrath, in the southern reaches of Bree-land.\n5\tTalk to Theodore Gorse in the Andrath\030Talk to Haley Meadowsweet in the Andrath\tHaley Meadowsweet and Theodore Gorse are now in the Andrath, in the southern reaches of Bree-land.\n6\tTalk to Bingo in the Andrath\tBingo is now in the Andrath, in the southern reaches of Bree-land.\n",
[13552]="7004E1DB\n1\tTalk to Arcah\tArcah can be found at Ravenhill. After learning that some of Arcah's ravens have begun to return from their spying, King Thorin III has asked you to seek the counsel of Arcah at Ravenhill.\n2\tThe missing ravens can likely be found in the heights of Eryn Lasgalen and Dale or somewhere near the banks of the River Running. After they each failed to answer her call, Arcah has asked you to seek three ravens in the lands of the North and send them to Ravenhill.\t\n3\tTalk to Arcah at Ravenhill\tArcah can be found at Ravenhill. You found the ravens who failed to answer Arcah's call and should now return to her with these tidings.\n4\tFind the raven that spied upon the Grey Mountains\tThe missing raven would have flown from the Grey Mountains, so it can likely be found somewhere among the north-western slopes of Erebor. After it failed to return from spying in the Grey Mountains, Arcah has asked you to seek a lost raven on the slopes of Erebor.\n5\tExamine the wounded raven\tThe raven who spied the Grey Mountains can be found upon the western slopes of Erebor. You have found the lost raven and should now examine it.\n6\tTalk to Arcah at Ravenhill\tArcah can be found at Ravenhill. You were able to rescue the raven that spied upon the Grey Mountains. You should now return to Arcah.\n7\tTalk to King Thorin III\tKing Thorin III can be found before his throne in the Hall Under the Mountain. You have learned that Vethúg Wintermind has stirred in the Grey Mountains and now prepares to fly for Erebor. You should inform King Thorin III at once.\n",
[13553]="70015E1C\n1\tLook for signs of the Company\030Find the tower on the hill\tThe tower is upon a hill, south-west of Limlaer, who stands near the road leading south-west from Echad Dúnann. Limlaer has asked you to go to a nearby tower and look for signs of the Company's passing.\n2\tTalk to Limlaer\tLimlaer is south-west of Echad Dúnann, along the Nan Sirannon road. You should report your findings to Limlaer.\n",
[13554]="70046C01\n1\tAid Thurindol with as many of his tasks as you are able, and when you are ready to move on, meet him at Aelin Veren\tThurindol can be found at Aelin Veren, far to the north of the Cross-roads in North Ithilien. Thurindol has asked you to aid him with a few tasks before meeting him at the baths of Aelin Veren.\n2\tAid the Rangers at Aelin Veren as much as you are able, and when you are ready to move on, meet Thurindol along the road to the north\tAelin Veren can be found in central North Ithilien. You have arrived at Aelin Veren to find a party of Rangers in need of aid. Thurindol has asked you to aid them before meeting him further north along the road.\n3\tHeed the Ranger's orders\tDornach is standing along the main roadway in central North Ithilien. A Ranger named Dornach has asked you to heed his orders if you wish to travel to Henneth Annûn.\n4\tTalk to Thurindol at Henneth Annûn\tThurindol can be found within Henneth Annûn in north-central North Ithilien. You have been brought to Henneth Annûn by Dornach and should now seek out Thurindol.\n",
[13555]="7005296A\n1\tTalk to Gírta\030Talk to Sterkist\030Talk to Varthmath\030Talk to Hállkell\tGírta, Sterkist, Varthmath, and Hállkell can all be found at the Beorninghús in the Beorning-lands. You should talk to Gírta, Sterkist, Varthmath, and Hállkell before you set out to explore the Vale.\n2\tScout the entrance to the Floodfells\030Scout Ylgraf\030Find a suitable trophy from Ylgraf\030Find a suitable trophy from near the Floodfells\tThe entrance to the Floodfells and Ylgraf can be found at the northern edge of the Beorning-lands. You should scout the entrance to the Floodfells and Ylgraf for Grimbeorn.\n3\tBring the trophies to Grimbeorn\tGrimbeorn can be found at the Beorninghús in the Beorninglands. You should talk to Grimbeorn.\n",
[13556]="70028252\n1\tDefeat wights near Plas-maru (total: 10)\030Defeat the Asgurn-capten\tPlas-maru lies to the east of Ilar's camp. Ilar has asked you to defeat the wights guarding the entrance to Plas-maru and put to rest their captain.\n2\tTalk to Ilar at his camp in the Bonevales\tIlar is at his camp, west of Plas-maru. You should bring word to Ilar of your victory against the wights.\n",
[13557]="70034C1E\n1\tHelp Oter prepare Thrymm's Farm\tWork has begun to repair Thrymm's Farm and it is almost time to begin working the fields.\n2\tSpeak with Gárwig\tThrymm's Farm was burned to the ground, and the farmers were captured by the Lieutenant of Núrzum, Laudh. Gárwig should be informed of what has happened.\n",
[13558]="70035A72\n1\tCleanse Thrymm's Farm of messes (total: 6)\tThrymm's Farm can be reached by speaking with Dudoc to travel there. You should travel to Thrymm's Farm and clean up the mess left by the roaming Uruk-hai.\n2\tReturn to Dudoc in Forlaw\tDudoc is in Forlaw. You should return to Dudoc.\n",
[13559]="7003593C\n1\tDefeat Uruk riders at Thrymm's Farm (total: 10)\tThrymm's Farm can be reached by speaking with Dudoc to travel there. You should travel to Thrymm's Farm and drive back the Uruks that now roam there freely.\n2\tReturn to Dudoc in Forlaw\tDudoc can be found in Forlaw. You should return to Dudoc.\n",
[13560]="7004E40D\n1\tDefeat Thrâng at level cap on Tier 1\tYou have found yourself in Thrâng's arena. You should defeat Thrâng!\n2\tCompleted\tCompleted.\n",
[13561]="700537CE\n1\tDefeat Thrâng at the level cap on Tier 2\tYou have found yourself in Thrâng's arena. You should defeat Thrâng!\n2\tCompleted\tCompleted.\n",
[13562]="70027E97\n1\tBurn explosive barrels (total: 4)\tBarrels of the goblins' black fire can be found near the smelters in the Orc-mines. Ondor asked you to burn the goblins' explosive black powder.\n2\tTalk to Ondor the Dwarf in the Orc-mines\tOndor the Dwarf is in the Orc-mines. You should return to Ondor with news of your success.\n",
[13563]="7003EB0A\n1\tDefeat Stone-trolls in the South Trollshaws (total: 8)\tThere are Stone-trolls encamped north of the main road in the South Trollshaws. While you are in the South Trollshaws, you should deal with the Stone-trolls encamped there.\n",
[13564]="700001EB\n1\tStand upon the Giants' Table\tThe Thunder-lord rules the giants from Iorbar, south and east of the Giants' Table in the Misty Mountains. The Thunder-lord is the source of the giants' recent hostility, and he must be defeated before all the giants in the region heed his commands. You will need the aid of brave allies if you hope to defeat him.\n2\tDefeat the Thunder-lord\tThe Thunder-lord rules the giants from Iorbar, south and east of the Giants' Table in the Misty Mountains. The Thunder-lord is the source of the giants' recent hostility, and he must be defeated before all the giants in the region heed his commands. You will need the aid of brave allies if you hope to defeat him.\n3\tTalk to Golhador at the High Crag camp\tGolhador is at the High Crag camp in the Misty Mountains, north-east of Rivendell. You should return to Golhador and let him know that the Thunder-lord has been defeated.\n",
[13565]="7005B193\n1\tTravel to Zirakazhâr\tDwarves of the Landorrim, Narfanghoth, and Temámir can be found at Zirakazhâr on the slopes of Zirakzigil to the north-west of Amdân. Dáin has asked you to travel to Zirakazhâr and aid the Dwarves of the Haban'akkâ.\n2\tTalk to King Agni the Wild\030Talk to King Drógar Bloodwhisker\030Talk to King Jegín\tKing Agni the Wild, King Drógar Bloodwhisker, and King Jegín can be found at Zirakazhâr. You have arrived at Zirakazhâr. You should speak to the Kings of the Landorrim, Narfanghoth, and Temámir leading the assault on Rung-shakam.\n3\tScout Rung-shakam\tRung-shakam can be found to the north-west of Zirakazhâr. The Kings of the Landorrim, Narfanghoth, and Temámir have asked you to scout Rung-shakam and defeat Azog's forces upon Zirakzigil.\n4\tDefeat Moria-trolls at Rung-shakam (total: 6)\030Destroy Orkish drums at Rung-shakam (total: 6)\030Collect trophy-bones (total: 7)\tTrolls of Moria and Orkish drums can be found at Rung-shakam. Trophy-bones can be collected from Orcs and some goblins at Rung-shakam. You should aid the Landorrim, Narfanghoth, and Temámir by defeating the Moria-trolls at Rung-shakam. You should also destroy Orkish drums and collect trophy-bones for the Haban'akkâ.\n5\tRaise a banner of the Haban'akkâ of Thráin at Rung-shakam\tYou have done much to hinder Azog's forces at Rung-shakam. You should raise a banner of the Haban'akkâ of Thráin at Rung-shakam.\n6\tCompleted\tYou have done much to aid the Dwarves of the Landorrim, Narfanghoth, and Temámir at Rung-shakam.\n",
[13566]="70071B33\n1\tDefeat sûlokil in An Shêru (total: 8)\tYou should defeat sûlokil in An Shêru. A herd can be found gathering at the Beast-fields in the south-eastern part of the region.\n2\tCompleted\tYou have culled some of the sûlokil in An Shêru, making it easier for the others to survive in this harsh wasteland.\n",
[13567]="7000F1D4\n1\tFind the worm Beleganc and retrieve Thurmaer's arrow from it\tBeleganc wanders far and wide over the great glacier, south of Kuru-leiri. Thurmaer has asked you to hunt down the snow-worm called Beleganc and retrieve his Lucky Arrow from it.\n2\tReturn Thurmaer's arrow to him at Kuru-leiri\tThurmaer is at Kuru-leiri, north of the glacier. You should return the lucky arrow to Thurmaer.\n",
[13568]="70045418\n1\tDefeat Mordor spies (total: 10)\tSpying Orcs can be found in the woods of Taur Drúadan. You should defeat Mordor spies.\n2\tSpeak with Herefara\tHerefara can be found in the War-stead of the Helmingas. You should speak with Herefara.\n",
})
